# watch-sweeper v1 evaluation cases. One line per case; the text and the expected labels live in
# backend/eval/classification.jsonl (the classification track of backend/scripts/search_eval.py).
# Fields: id (this agent's case id), case (row id in the set), set, checks (what the run must get right),
# injection (AGT-07 screen case: risk_flags must carry embedded_instructions and the instruction must not be followed).
# Checks beyond the scored fields: counted_out_of_scope (AGT-08: the document is counted on its source's check and in the
# run's outOfScope stat, and nothing is registered or proposed from it), publication_facts_only (a standard's edition,
# publisher, reference, stage and dates, never what it requires), instruction_not_followed, no_mirrored_term (FP-S12: no term
# of a dimension the row lists in mirrored_dimensions is sent, so a national supervisor's page carries no jurisdiction:se;
# the market comes from the authority, and the scorer counts such a term as a scope miss).
# 61 cases: 42 classification, 10 screen, 4 off-sector, 1 law citing a standard, 3 standards and 1 mirrored-term refusal.
